  "id": "Compound::DB00860 - Gene::4306",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is linked to Nr3c2 through a shared pathway involving Fludrocortisone, which binds to Nr3c2. This relationship is supported by the evidence that Prednisolone causes both alkalosis hypokalaemic and increased insulin requirement, both of which are mediated by Fludrocortisone. The lowest common ancestor of these entities is 21-Hydroxy Steroid and Therapeutic Glucocorticoid, suggesting a broader pharmacological context. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Prednisolone influences Nr3c2 through Fludrocortisone, possibly via a common regulatory pathway. The evidence suggests a direct or indirect interaction between Prednisolone and Nr3c2, mediated by Fludrocortisone, which may be relevant in the context of glucocorticoid action and its downstream effects.",
